const ct = req.headers.get("content-type") ?? "";
if (ct.includes("application/json")) {
  const j = await req.json().catch(() => ({}));
  id_turno = Number(j.id_turno);
} else {
  const f = await req.formData();
  id_turno = Number(f.get("id_turno"));
}
...
// error return JSON for json; for form → redirect to /reserva/id?error=...
// success: for json → return { init_point }; form → redirect 303 to init_point
```

OK note it for the route implementation.

Also the reserva page innocently exposes the server-only `process.env.MP_ACCESS_TOKEN` state to client via prop (boolean) — that's fine.

Wait, "PagarMP" uses server-rendered form → good, no client component needed.

Now APIs. Files:

